rcuit breakers you'll intuit  circuit breakers you'll find it  so  circuit breakers is a tool at intuit  that  automates the  data flow based on some quality checks  circuit breakers allows you to define  conditions under which data is not fit  for use  and it automatically stops the pipeline  and says nope this data is bad i don't  trust it if i keep the data flowing then  there's going to be consequences  downstream  what principles  is this touching well embracing risk  data is going to break  they have accepted the fact that data is  going to break so they need to do  something about it  they automate the stopping of the  process this isn't an alert that gets  sent to a data engineer who then has to  wake up at 2 am and push a button to  stop a pipeline because nobody ever  wants to do that and then you're going  to forget to turn on the pipeline again  and then the data stale and you have an  even bigger problem  so automating the  start and stop process of the pipeline  is really important in this case  especially at the scale that intuit is  operating at  and finally favoring simplicity this is  a diagram from their blog post it's two  boxes  this is about as simple of a process and  a tool as you can get data is bad stop  the flow data is good start the flow  you don't need a complex system  in order to start practicing and having  better highly higher reliable reliable  data  midas from airbnb  so  midas is a way for uh that airbnb allows  you to certify data sets as effectively  golden  part as of the certification process  includes understanding  what uh what does the data mean  does it actually  comply with the expectations of the  business for that data  and also tracking the reliability and  accuracy of over time because if it  becomes less reliable  then it shouldn't be a golden data set  so  this is actually much more interesting  because this is less automation this is  much more  policy this is a lot more about the  practices that the organization 